<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand von Hompesch zu Bolheim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1744–1805</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand von Hompesch zu Bolheim was the last Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a>, and the first German to hold the office, elected in 1797. In June 1798 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s fleet, on its way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, demanded entry, and Hompesch surrendered the island without serious resistance. He left Malta, abdicated in 1799 and died in poverty at Montpellier.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-von-hompesch-zu-bolheim.jpg" alt="Ferdinand von Hompesch zu Bolheim" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ferdinand_von_Hompesch_zu_Bolheim,_71st_and_last_Grand_Master_of_the_Hospitallers_of_the_Order_of_St._John_of_Jerusalem_(French_School,_18th-century).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
